         https://metacpan.org/release/HAMT
 
 
+XPERL COMPATIBILITY
+
+Custom read ops use XSPP_wrapped when PERL_RC_STACK is enabled. This gives
+their traditional stack macros an uncounted stack slice and releases the
+arguments when the op returns. Older Perl builds keep the original path.
+
+On XPerl, callback walks identify last and next by the structured diagnostic
+code and control-word parameter, independently of diagnostic rendering.
+Other errors are propagated as their original objects. The structured-error
+branch is guarded by XPERL_VERSION. Ordinary Perl keeps its string handling.
+
+Reference-count probes measure the entry's increment within one XS call.
+An absolute count taken in Perl also includes references held by an RC
+argument stack and cannot be compared directly with a count inside XS.
+
